நிண","parts":[{"text":"கொழுநிண","lemma":"கொழுநிண","gloss":"rich fat"}],"gloss":"rich fat","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாற்றம்","parts":[{"text":"நாற்றம்","lemma":"nāṟṟam","gloss":"aroma"}],"gloss":"aroma"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மறுகுடன்","parts":[{"text":"மறுகு","lemma":"maṟuku","gloss":"street"},{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"uṭaṉ","gloss":"along with"}],"gloss":"all over the street"},{"surface":"கமழும்","parts":[{"text":"கமழும்","lemma":"kamaḻ","gloss":"spreading fragrance"}],"gloss":"spreading fragrance"},{"surface":"மதுகை","parts":[{"text":"மதுகை","lemma":"matukai","gloss":"strength/courage"}],"gloss":"strong"},{"surface":"மன்றத்து","parts":[{"text":"மன்றத்து","lemma":"மன்றத்து","gloss":"in the common ground"}],"gloss":"in the common ground","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அலந்தலை","parts":[{"text":"அலந்தலை","lemma":"alantalai","gloss":"shabby-topped"}],"gloss":"shabby-topped"},{"surface":"இரத்தி","parts":[{"text":"இரத்தி","lemma":"iratti","gloss":"jujube tree"}],"gloss":"jujube tree"},{"surface":"அலங்குபடு","parts":[{"text":"அலங்கு","lemma":"alaṅku","gloss":"swaying"},{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"falling"}],"gloss":"swaying"},{"surface":"நீழல்","parts":[{"text":"நீழல்","lemma":"nīḻal","gloss":"shade"}],"gloss":"shade"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கயந்தலை","parts":[{"text":"கயம்","lemma":"kayam","gloss":"tender"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"talai","gloss":"head"}],"gloss":"tender-headed"},{"surface":"சிறாஅர்","parts":[{"text":"சிறாஅர்","lemma":"ciṟāar","gloss":"children"}],"gloss":"children"},{"surface":"கணை","parts":[{"text":"கணை","lemma":"kaṇai","gloss":"toy arrow"}],"gloss":"toy arrows"},{"surface":"விளையாடும்","parts":[{"text":"விளையாடும்","lemma":"viḷaiyāṭu","gloss":"playing"}],"gloss":"playing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருமிளை","parts":[{"text":"அரு","lemma":"aru","gloss":"difficult"},{"text":"மிளை","lemma":"miḷai","gloss":"protective forest"}],"gloss":"difficult protective forest"},{"surface":"இருக்கை","parts":[{"text":"இருக்கை","lemma":"irukkai","gloss":"settlement"}],"gloss":"settlement"},{"surface":"அதுவே","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"that"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"that indeed is"},{"surface":"வென்வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வென்வேல்","lemma":"வென்வேல்","gloss":"victorious spear"}],"gloss":"victorious spear","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ūr","gloss":"town"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"the town indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the area of open land where male elephants bathed in dust, / because the unseasonable great rain poured within limits and passed, / due to drinking the tawny-colored scanty water held in pits, / the muddy spring water where branches were placed to block, / he who takes his turn drinks, living a frugal life. / Men of truthful words who killed porcupines, / on the leaf-gate with a slender latch-bar where they sliced the fat of monitor lizards, / in order to make portions in the front yard of their small house, / the aroma of rich fat roasted with a firebrand / spreads all over the street, in the common ground of strength, / under the swaying shade of the shabby-topped jujube tree, / tender-headed children play with toy arrows. / That indeed is the settlement in the difficult protective forest, the town of the victorious spear!","translation":"In the open lands where male elephants once bathed in dust, unseasonable heavy rains have poured and passed, leaving scanty, tawny water in the hollows. To filter this muddy spring water, they have blocked it with branches, and the people drink it in turns, living a frugal life. These are men of unfailing words who hunt porcupines. In the front yards of their small houses, behind leaf-gates with slender latch-bars, they slice the fat of monitor lizards to share. The rich aroma of fat roasted on firebrands spreads all over the street. In the common ground of this strong settlement, under the swaying shade of shabby-topped jujube trees, tender-headed children play with toy arrows. Such is this settlement protected by a dense forest, the town of the victorious spear!","modern":"ஆண் யானைகள் புழுதியில் விளையாடிய வெட்டவெளி நிலப்பகுதியில், புதிய பெருமழை பெய்து ஓய்ந்ததால், பள்ளங்களில் தேங்கியுள்ள செந்நிறமான குறைந்த நீரை மக்கள் குடிக்கிறார்கள். கிளைகளைக் கொண்டு தடுத்து வடிகட்டிய அந்தச் சேறு கலந்த ஊற்றுநீரை, முறை வைத்துக்கொண்டு பகிர்ந்து குடிக்கும் எளிய வாழ்க்கை அவர்களுடையது. முள்ளம்பன்றிகளைக் கொன்று வேட்டையாடும், சொன்ன சொல் தவறாத ஆடவர்கள் அவர்கள். உடும்பின் கொழுப்பை வெட்டி, சிறிய வீடுகளின் முற்றத்தில் பங்கிட்டுக் கொள்வதற்காகக் கொள்ளிக்கட்டையால் சுடுகிறார்கள். அந்த நெய்க்கொழுப்பின் வாசனை தெருவெங்கும் வீசுகிறது. வலிமைமிக்க அந்த ஊர் மன்றத்தில், வாடிய உச்சியை உடைய இலந்தை மரத்தின் அசையும் நிழலில், மென்மையான தலையை உடைய சிறுவர்கள் அம்புகளை எய்து விளையாடுகிறார்கள். அரிய காவற்காட்டை எல்லையாகக் கொண்ட அந்தப் போர்வீரர்களின் குடியிருப்புதான், வெற்றிவேலை உடைய தலைவனின் ஊராகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the vākai tiṇai (victory/bravery) and vallāṇ mullai tuṟai (the strength and hospitality of a warrior's home). The poet, Uṟaiyūr Mutukaṇṇaṉ Cāttaṉār, describes the rugged yet self-sufficient life of a warrior settlement situated in a dry, forested region. The inhabitants live a frugal life, drinking muddy water in turns from a spring filtered with branches, yet they are rich in courage and generosity. The men are skilled hunters who bring home porcupines and monitor lizards, roasting the fat to share with the entire village, filling the streets with the aroma of meat. In the common ground, under the shade of jujube trees, children play with toy arrows, showing that bravery and martial skill are nurtured from childhood. The poem praises the chief's village, protected by a dense forest, as a place of true strength and hospitality.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.74],[0.81,1.1],[1.18,1.62],[1.7,1.9],[1.9,3.2],[3.2,3.4],[3.4,4.4],[4.4,4.8],[4.8,5.0],[5.0,5.9],[5.9,6.8],[6.88,7.1],[7.1,7.58],[